  "body": "Tucked away in one of Auckland's most tightly held waterfront locations, 94 Stanley Point Road is a home of exceptional design and understated elegance. Positioned between a small public park and a private estate, it enjoys a remarkable sense of peace, privacy and connection to the water.\r\n\r\nDesigned by acclaimed New Zealand architects Architectus, under the direction of Patrick Clifford, the home was awarded the prestigious New Zealand Institute of Architects Supreme Award for Architecture. More than 30 years on, its thoughtful design and timeless simplicity remain as impressive as ever.\r\n\r\nBeautifully integrated into its natural surroundings, the architecture celebrates light, space and the changing coastal landscape. Generous living areas connect effortlessly with sheltered outdoor terraces, capturing all-day sun and expansive north-facing views across the water. Whether entertaining friends or enjoying a quiet morning coffee, there is a space for every occasion.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation is equally considered, offering four generous bedrooms, three bathrooms, a powder room and dedicated office. A fully self-contained studio provides wonderful flexibility for guests, extended family or working from home, while a separate parents' wing offers a peaceful retreat.\r\n\r\nA superb entertainer's kitchen anchors the main living spaces, while radiator heating ensures comfort throughout the seasons. Natural materials, beautifully framed outlooks and an abundance of birdlife create an atmosphere that is both sophisticated and wonderfully relaxed.\r\n\r\nJust below the property, the sheltered bay invites morning swims and time spent enjoying the water. Yet despite the feeling of complete escape, Auckland's CBD remains easily accessible by ferry or bus.\r\n\r\nTimeless architecture. Absolute tranquility. A waterfront lifestyle like no other.",
